TI  - New Fairness Metrics for Recommendation that Embrace Differences
PY  - 2017
UR  - https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.09838
N1  - arXiv:1706.09838
AB  - We study fairness in collaborative-filtering recommender systems, which are sensitive to discrimination that exists in historical data. Biased data can lead collaborative filtering methods to make unfair predictions against minority groups of users. We identify the insufficiency of existing fairness metrics and propose four new metrics that address different forms of unfairness.
